{"id": "obs:anavasthitatva", "name": "Instability (anavasthitatva)", "category": "obstacle", "description": "The mind's not being established in a level it has gained. One of the nine obstacles (1.30, YBh 1.30).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "1.30", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:1.30"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "1.30", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:1.30"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:ekatattva-abhyasa", "prc:isvara-pranidhana"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:viksepa-sahabhuva", "name": "The five accompaniments of distraction", "category": "meditation-fault", "description": "Pain (threefold), dejection, trembling of the limbs, and [disturbed] inhalation and exhalation accompany the distractions; they occur in the distracted, not the concentrated, mind (1.31, YBh 1.31).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "1.31", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:1.31"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "1.31", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:1.31"]}], "members": ["duḥkha", "daurmanasya", "aṅgamejayatva", "śvāsa", "praśvāsa"], "antidotes": ["prc:ekatattva-abhyasa"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:five-klesas", "name": "The five afflictions (kleśa)", "category": "affliction", "description": "Ignorance, I-am-ness, attachment, aversion and clinging to life (2.3), rooted in ignorance (2.4), the root of the karmic residue (2.12).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.3", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.3"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.4", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.4"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.12", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.12"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.3", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.3"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.4", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.4"]}], "members": ["obs:avidya", "obs:asmita", "obs:raga", "obs:dvesa", "obs:abhinivesa"], "antidotes": ["prc:kriya-yoga (thins them, 2.2)", "prc:dhyana (removes their gross activities, 2.11)", "involution (pratiprasava) for the subtle (2.10)", "prc:viveka-khyati"], "equivalents": [{"target": "obs:klesa", "grade": "partial", "note": "Same word as the Buddhist defilements; Yoga's list of five differs from Buddhist lists", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.3"]}], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:avidya", "name": "Ignorance (avidyā)", "category": "affliction", "description": "Taking the impermanent, impure, painful and non-self as permanent, pure, pleasant and self (2.5); the field of the other afflictions (2.4); cause of the conjunction (2.24); not absence of knowledge but a contrary cognition (YBh 2.5).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.4", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.4"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.5", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.5"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.24", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.24"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.5", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.5"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:viveka-khyati"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:asmita", "name": "I-am-ness (asmitā)", "category": "affliction", "description": "The seeming identity of the power of seeing with the seer (2.6, YBh 2.6).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.6", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.6"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.6", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.6"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:viveka-khyati"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:raga", "name": "Attachment (rāga)", "category": "affliction", "description": "Attachment follows on pleasure (2.7).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.7", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.7"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "1.11", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:1.11"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:vairagya"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:dvesa", "name": "Aversion (dveṣa)", "category": "affliction", "description": "Aversion follows on pain (2.8).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.8", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.8"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "1.11", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:1.11"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:four-attitudes", "prc:pratipaksa-bhavana"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:abhinivesa", "name": "Clinging to life (abhiniveśa)", "category": "affliction", "description": "Flowing by its own momentum, rooted even in the wise; the wish 'may I not cease, may I be', a fear of death found even in the newborn (2.9, YBh 2.9).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.9", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.9"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.9", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.9"]}], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:vitarka-himsadi", "name": "Harmful thoughts (vitarka): violence and the rest", "category": "passion", "description": "Thoughts of violence, untruth, stealing, incontinence and possessiveness, done, caused or approved, from greed, anger or delusion, mild to intense; their fruit is endless suffering and ignorance (2.33–34, YBh 2.33–34).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.33", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.33"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.34", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.34"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.33", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.33"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.34", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.34"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:pratipaksa-bhavana"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:lobha-krodha-moha", "name": "Greed, anger and delusion as roots of harmful thoughts", "category": "poison", "description": "Harmful thoughts are preceded by greed, anger or delusion (2.34): violence for meat or skin, from 'he wronged me', or from 'it will be merit for me' (YBh 2.34); the karmic residue arises from desire, greed, delusion and anger (YBh 2.12).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.34", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.34"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.12", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.12"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.34", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.34"]}], "members": ["lobha", "krodha", "moha"], "antidotes": ["prc:pratipaksa-bhavana"], "equivalents": [{"target": "obs:three-poisons", "grade": "partial", "note": "Parallels the Buddhist three roots (lobha, dosa, moha); the second member differs (krodha, anger, vs dosa, hatred)", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.34"]}], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:siddhis-as-upasarga", "name": "Powers as obstacles in samādhi (upasarga)", "category": "meditation-fault", "description": "Intuition and the divine senses, arising in the concentrated mind, are obstacles because they oppose seeing; they count as powers only in emergence (3.37, YBh 3.37).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "3.37", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:3.37"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "3.37", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:3.37"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:vairagya"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:sanga-smaya", "name": "Attachment and pride at the celestials' invitation", "category": "meditation-fault", "description": "At the honey stage the gods invite the yogin with pleasures, elixirs, sky-cars and nymphs; attachment would make him fuel for saṃsāra again, and pride ('even the gods desire me') lets carelessness revive the afflictions (3.51, YBh 3.51).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "3.51", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:3.51"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "3.51", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:3.51"]}], "antidotes": ["reflection on the faults of attachment (YBh 3.51)", "prc:vairagya"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:prakasavarana", "name": "The covering of the light (prakāśāvaraṇa)", "category": "impurity", "description": "The karma that covers discriminative knowledge, yoking luminous sattva to what should not be done; it dwindles through prāṇāyāma (2.52, YBh 2.52) and is destroyed by the great bodiless concentration (3.43).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.52", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.52"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "3.43", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:3.43"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.52", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.52"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:pranayama"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:asuddhi", "name": "Impurity (aśuddhi)", "category": "impurity", "description": "Impurity — fivefold error — variegated by beginningless karma, afflictions and tendencies (YBh 2.1, 2.28); destroyed by the practice of the limbs (2.28) and by austerity (2.43).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.28", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.28"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "2.43", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:2.43"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.1", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.1"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "2.28", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:2.28"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:tapas", "prc:yama", "prc:niyama"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:vyutthana-samskara", "name": "Impressions of emergence (vyutthāna-saṃskāra)", "category": "meditation-fault", "description": "Impressions of the outgoing mind that compete with those of stilling (3.9) and overpower them when the latter are weak (YBh 3.10); the impression born of samādhi-insight obstructs them (YBh 1.50).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "3.9", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:3.9"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "3.10", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:3.10"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "1.50", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:1.50"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:abhyasa"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:pratyayantara", "name": "Other cognitions in the gaps of discernment", "category": "meditation-fault", "description": "In the gaps of a mind flowing with discernment, cognitions such as 'I am', 'mine', 'I know', 'I do not know' arise from dwindling impressions (4.27, YBh 4.27); they are removed as the afflictions are (4.28).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "4.27", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:4.27"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "4.28", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:4.28"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "4.27", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:4.27"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:viveka-khyati"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:prakrtilaya-short-of-kaivalya", "name": "Absorption in prakṛti or the bodiless state short of kaivalya", "category": "meditation-fault", "description": "The bodiless and those merged in prakṛti experience a state 'as if' of kaivalya but return when their impressions ripen or the mind's unfinished task draws it back (1.19, YBh 1.19); lower dispassion includes giving up the wish for these states (YBh 1.15).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-sutra", "ref": "1.19", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-sutra:1.19"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "1.15", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:1.15"]}, {"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "1.19", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:1.19"]}], "antidotes": ["prc:vairagya", "prc:viveka-khyati"], "notes": "Framed as an obstacle by this unit on the basis of YBh 1.15 and 1.19; the sūtra itself only states the cause of their state.", "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
{"id": "obs:ksipta-mudha-viksipta", "name": "The scattered, stupefied and distracted mind", "category": "meditation-fault", "description": "The first three of the five levels of mind; samādhi in the distracted mind, subordinate to distraction, does not count as yoga (YBh 1.1).", "lineages": ["lin:patanjala-yoga"], "sources": [{"source": "src:yoga-bhasya", "ref": "1.1", "rests_on": ["tea:yoga-bhasya:1.1"]}], "members": ["kṣipta", "mūḍha", "vikṣipta"], "antidotes": ["prc:kriya-yoga", "prc:abhyasa"], "coverage": ["A5", "D"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}}
